From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Kostersitz <mkostersitz@mac.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:47:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: a gesture acts on the screen it started on, and the
 overview opens there

On a Duo with the two panel window policy a gesture made on one screen has to act on that screen: its app (or home),
whichever screen holds window focus, and a recents list opened by the gesture lays out on that screen.

- TouchInteractionService remembers which screen the gesture started on (DuoPanels) and restricts the running task
  to the one on that screen (TopTaskTracker.CachedTaskInfo.restrictedToPanel).
- With home on one screen and an app on the other Launcher stays resumed, which made every gesture a launcher gesture;
  a gesture on the screen that runs an app now goes to that app (InputConsumerUtils).
- The overview is laid out for, and sized to, the screen the gesture started on.
- The size of the whole display comes from DisplayController: the size of the touch service window follows the
  screen that holds focus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
